insert into public.chapters (series_id, season_number, week, day, script, meta) values
('dark-moon', 1, 3, 1, $json${"week":3,"day":1,"title":"Somewhere warm","heading":"Somewhere warm","question":"a girl was held here too, and moved \"somewhere warm\". Who is she, and where is that?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"*Somewhere warm.*\n\nThe words are still hanging in the lamplight. Corin is watching you, to see what you will do with them. He holds his bandaged hand in his lap, palm up, the way somebody told him to keep it."},{"t":"act","label":"KNEEL DOWN TO HIM"},{"t":"say","text":"He thinks hard, the way children do when they know it matters.\n\n*\"Wren.\"*\n\n*\"She said home was always warm. The ground's warm, and the hills are all black, and everything smells like a fire that went out a long time ago. She missed it.\"*\n\nA pause.\n\n*\"She said they told her she was going home first.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"The ledger is opened to its newest page, and held flat under the lamp. Four names. Beside the third, in that same small, careful hand: *Wren — Ashcombe.*\n\nIn Meira's satchel the same name turns up in her own neat hand, on her list of children she was worried for. Beside it is a knot of her shorthand. Garrick tilts the page to the light and reads the knot off without a pause.\n\n*\"Ashcombe's a shepherds' village on the edge of the burned country,\"* he says. *\"A long day west. And above it she's marked a place. The Blackglass.\"*"},{"t":"act","label":"ASK ABOUT THE FOURTH NAME"},{"t":"say","text":"Beside the fourth name is a place far to the north.\n\n*\"One road at a time. The girl's is the one with tracks on it.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"The night wears down. By the grey before dawn you are all out at the mouth of the old shaft, with Corin half asleep against somebody's shoulder and the hillside wet and colourless round you.\n\nThen something comes up out of the hill behind you.\n\nOne of them. Alone, hood back, with a blade."},{"t":"fight","name":"THE ONE WHO CAME UP AFTER YOU","desc":"He does not say what he wants.","firstLines":null,"strikeFirst":{"on":"player"}},{"t":"say","text":"He does not say a word. He breaks away over the shoulder of the hill and is gone, the way the others have gone: the first gap, and no sound.\n\nFor a few breaths you can hear him on the scree below, quick and sure-footed in the half-light. Then there is only the wind in the wet grass."},{"t":"say","text":"He leaves the hill with a limp he did not bring to it.","cond":{"on":"fight","won":true}},{"t":"say","text":"Below the shaft, in the wet grass, the tracks are plain to anyone who looks."},{"t":"act","label":"LOOK"},{"t":"say","text":"One cart, lightly loaded, two hours old at most. Two walkers beside it. And a third set of prints, small, stepping where it is told.\n\nThey turn west."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"The cart is riding light.","second":"They are hauling nothing but her."},"Agility":{"first":"The small prints keep exactly to the walkers' pace.","second":"She is not being dragged. She is doing as she is told."},"Intellect":{"first":"They left by the road, in the open, at a walk.","second":"People who think they are hunted do not travel like this."},"Charm":{"first":"Corin has not let go of somebody's sleeve since you came out of the hill.","second":"He is afraid you will not be there when he looks."},"Craft":{"first":"The left wheel pulls.","second":"The same cart, again."},"Aim":{"first":"West, without a turn in it as far as you can see.","second":"They know exactly where they are going."}}},{"t":"say","text":"On the walk down, riding on {F2}'s shoulders, Corin says your names over to himself, one by one, the way you would tie a knot to keep it."},{"t":"say","text":"You hear the mill before you see it: the slow knock of the wheel, still going round over nothing.\n\nBy mid-morning you have carried him down the valley to the mill. His mother sees him from the yard before you are halfway across the field, and the sound she makes is one none of you will forget.\n\nShe does not thank you. She cannot yet. She holds him, with the white linen on his palm pressed between them, and looks at each of you over his head, one after another, as if she is learning your faces by heart.\n\nCorin tells her your names. He has not forgotten one."},{"t":"say","text":"Where the west road leaves the valley, a wayside shrine stands older than the road: a stub of carved stone with the carving worn off. Somebody has left a sprig of heather at its foot, long since gone brown."},{"t":"act","label":"FEEL BEHIND IT"},{"t":"say","text":"Cold as a coin left out in frost.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"They are not hiding her. They told her she was going home.\n\n**Why would anyone take a stolen child back to where she was born? Ashcombe: a long day west.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**SOMEWHERE WARM** · Day 1","You earned: `[gold]`","You learned: her name is **Wren**. \"Somewhere warm\" is home: **Ashcombe**, on the edge of the burned country. The ledger, Meira's list and the cart tracks all say so. Corin is home.","Fragment: 1 found, locked","Tomorrow: **Ashcombe, a long day west**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":24,"wAtk":17,"fightReward":300}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 3, 2, $json${"week":3,"day":2,"title":"Ashcombe","heading":"Ashcombe","question":"did Wren come home?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"On the second morning the west road climbs, and the grass along it grows thin and brown. Somewhere on the way the wind begins to smell of old smoke, though nothing is burning anywhere you can see.\n\nAshcombe sits where the green hills give out and the black ones begin: low stone houses, roofs weighted with slabs against the wind. The ground is warm underfoot, like a hearthstone the morning after. The springs run hot, and steam lifts off the trough by the first house.\n\nEvery door in the village shuts as you come up the street. Strangers took a child from here two weeks ago. You are strangers.\n\nOne door is the last to shut. Behind it, nobody moves away."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"Every roof here is held down with stones a man could barely lift.","second":"These are people used to holding on to things."},"Agility":{"first":"A curtain moves in every house but one.","second":"In that one, somebody is standing right behind the door."},"Intellect":{"first":"Two weeks since a child was taken, and nobody is out searching.","second":"They were told something that made searching seem useless."},"Charm":{"first":"The last door to shut, shut slowest.","second":"She wanted a longer look at you."},"Craft":{"first":"The well-rope is new, and the bucket is old.","second":"Somebody here still mends things. This is not a village that has given up."},"Aim":{"first":"At the end of the street the green stops, as if it had been cut with a knife.","second":"After that, everything is black."}}},{"t":"challenge","title":"THE LAST DOOR","desc":"She is on the other side of it, and she has not walked away.","options":[{"attr":"Charm","verb":"talk to her through the door until she opens it"},{"attr":"Intellect","verb":"know what will open it: the ledger's page, and her daughter's name in a stranger's hand"}],"reward":"+500g","fail":"the door stays shut, and you lose the day's light waiting"},{"t":"say","text":"A bolt draws back. The door opens a hand's width and stays there while she looks at you, one face at a time.\n\nThen it opens the rest of the way, and she stands back to let you in. The house smells of peat, and of bread that nobody has eaten.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"The door stays shut. The light goes off the street, and the shutters stay closed all down it.\n\nBut at dusk she comes out to your fire herself, with a shawl over her head, because nobody else in the world is looking for her daughter. You never see past her door.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"choice","id":0,"labels":["WHO TOOK HER?","WHY HER?","WHAT DID THEY SAY?"],"mode":"each","branches":[{"options":[0],"text":"*\"Two of them. Grey coats, good boots. Polite. They asked for her by name, and they knew the night she was born.\"*"},{"options":[1],"text":"She looks at the ground. *\"The night the moon went out. Here, a baby born on a night like that is given a chip of black glass off the hill, to keep the dark off. The old women pressed one into her fist before she'd even cried.\"*\n\nShe almost smiles. *\"She never lost it. She's picked up every chip she's found since. Her pockets rattle with them.\"*\n\nThe smile goes. *\"It didn't keep them off.\"*\n\nYou know that night. Every one of you was born on one like it."},{"options":[2],"text":"*\"He said they'd no wish to keep her. That they'd only need her the once.\"*\n\nShe says it the way you would repeat something you cannot make sense of.\n\n*\"He looked me in the eye when he said it. I've been lied to by better men than him. That wasn't what this was.\"*"}]},{"t":"say","text":"On the sill by the door, chips of black glass are set out in a row, smallest to largest, the way a child sets things out.\n\nThere is dust on the sill. There is none on the chips.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"At the well, a boy is selling polished chips of black glass off a board. He has been watching you the whole time. When the grown-ups have gone in he holds one out, and does not ask for the coin.\n\nThen, in a whisper, with one eye on the doors, he tells you what he saw. He was up after dark last night, where he should not have been. A cart came through the village without lamps. It did not stop. At the foot of the black road it was left standing empty, and whoever was in it went on up, on horses, toward the Blackglass.\n\nNobody has told her mother."},{"t":"say","text":"If Wren was in that cart, she passed within a mile of her own door."},{"t":"say","text":"Garrick knows the black road. *\"Where it forks, the shepherds take the left,\"* he says, and when he catches somebody looking at him, he nods up at the black hills. *\"My family's been in these hills longer than the roads have.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"At the edge of the village the pound wall, where the shepherds pen their flocks, is built on older stones than any house in Ashcombe: huge, square-cut, set without mortar. They are as warm as bread. All but one gap."},{"t":"act","label":"REACH INTO THE GAP"},{"t":"say","text":"The only cold thing in Ashcombe. Cold enough to ache the fingers.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"Above the last roof the black road goes up into the hills. As the evening comes on, the warm ground under the village ticks softly, cooling."},{"t":"say","text":"**What does anyone need a child for, once? The Blackglass: half a day up the black road, the place Meira marked.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**ASHCOMBE** · Day 2","You earned: `[gold]` · Charm or Intellect `[growth]`","You learned: **Wren did not come home.** Two polite men in grey coats took her two weeks ago: *\"they'd only need her the once.\"* Last night she was carried past her own village in the dark, and up the black road.","*On a failure:* You missed something in Ashcombe. Someone at the fire may have seen it.","You hold: a chip of black glass, from the boy at the well","Fragments: 2 found","Tomorrow: **the Blackglass, up the black road**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":24,"wAtk":17,"fightReward":0}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 3, 3, $json${"week":3,"day":3,"title":"The Blackglass","heading":"The Blackglass","question":"why the Blackglass? What is up there?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"Half a day up the black road, where the shepherds take the left fork, the hill opens out and you see it.\n\nThe Blackglass is a whole shoulder of hillside where the rock once ran like wax, and cooled: smooth, black, faintly rippled, as if a wave of stone had frozen halfway down the slope.\n\nNothing grows on it. The wind slides off it without a sound. The shepherds do not walk their flocks across it, and do not say why.\n\nMeira's page points to its far edge."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"The glass is warm through the soles of your boots.","second":"The heat is coming from underneath."},"Agility":{"first":"It is rippled, like sand under shallow water.","second":"The ripples all run one way. There is a grain to it."},"Intellect":{"first":"No lichen. No moss. Not one seed.","second":"Whatever burned this did more than burn it."},"Charm":{"first":"The shepherds never told you not to cross.","second":"They only stopped talking when you asked."},"Craft":{"first":"Glass like this takes the heat of a furnace.","second":"A whole hillside of it, all at once."},"Aim":{"first":"On all that smooth black there is one mark that is not a ripple.","second":"On the far side, just above the crack."}}},{"t":"challenge","title":"CROSS THE GLASS","desc":"It is slick as ice, and as warm as skin.","options":[{"attr":"Agility","verb":"straight over, and fast"},{"attr":"Aim","verb":"pick out the safe line from the edge, and take it slowly"}],"reward":"+500g","fail":"you go down hard, and slide"},{"t":"say","text":"You reach the far side clean, without once putting a hand to the glass. All the way over, a dark shape walks upside down beneath your boots: your own, in the black.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"You go down hard, and slide twenty feet before a ripple in the glass catches you. For a moment you lie still, with your cheek on the warm glass and your heart going. Bruised, shaken, and there all the same.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"say","text":"At the far edge the glass takes its toll. Where it has cracked, its edges are as sharp as knives, and you come off it with one boot split open along the sole.\n\nGarrick crosses last, the slow way, testing every step with the toe of his boot before he trusts it.\n\n*\"My knees have opinions about this glass. None of them good.\"*\n\nHe lowers himself onto the first rock he comes to, and rubs them."},{"t":"say","text":"Worn into the glass is a shape you know.\n\nBeside it, set into the rock as if the glass had cooled around it, is a housing of carved stone: old work, cut with the same care as the lock the dead man could not open, on the path upriver."},{"t":"act","label":"SET YOUR HAND TO IT"},{"t":"say","text":"It gives at the first touch. The glass round it holds the sun's warmth; the housing is a cold spot in it, and what is inside is colder still.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"Three children. Three marks.\n\nTamsin, at Fenmark, under the Widow's Tooth. Corin, at the mill. Wren, at Ashcombe, under the Blackglass.\n\nThe places Meira marked and the children in the ledger are one list."},{"t":"act","label":"WRITE IT IN HER NOTEBOOK"},{"t":"say","text":"It goes into Meira's notes, under her last entry, in your own hand. Your letters look clumsy under hers."},{"t":"say","text":"Hoof-scratches cross the glass a few yards from the mark, and run on, deeper into the burned country.\n\nThe riders did not even slow."},{"t":"press","title":"READ THE SCRATCHES","detail":"follow them to the edge of the glass","harder":4,"reward":"+200g, and one more detail"},{"t":"say","text":"Where the horses came off the glass the scratches bunch and deepen, and you can count them.\n\nSix horses. One of them is carrying double, and the second rider weighs almost nothing.","cond":{"on":"press"}},{"t":"say","text":"You camp in the lee of the glass, where the ground is warm enough to sleep on.\n\nThat evening, on Meira's plain page about the Blackglass, there is a line you all know, copied out in her hand: the first fragment any of you ever opened, *\"Five fell…\"* And squeezed into the margin beside it:\n\n*\"Five, the fragment says. Every other record I can find says four. I cannot find a fifth anywhere, and I have looked. A poet's count, perhaps — a number that sounded better than the truth.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"In the morning your split boot is whole again: the sole stitched back on, tight and neat, with waxed thread, while you slept. Garrick is winding what is left of the thread back onto its bobbin."},{"t":"act","label":"THANK HIM"},{"t":"say","text":"*\"Needed doing.\"*\n\nHe tucks the bobbin away inside his coat, and that is the end of it."},{"t":"say","text":"**They rode straight past the one thing Meira marked. So what are they riding to? On, into the black ridges.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE BLACKGLASS** · Day 3","You earned: `[gold]` · Agility or Aim `[growth]`","You learned: **three children, three marks.** Every child was taken from beside one of the places Meira marked. The riders passed this one without slowing.","Fragments: 3 found","Tomorrow: **the black ridges, on the riders' trail**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":24,"wAtk":17,"fightReward":0}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 3, 4, $json${"week":3,"day":4,"title":"The black ridges","heading":"The black ridges","question":"is she still alive?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"The burned country is ridge after ridge of black rock, under a sky that looks paler for it. The soil between the ridges is ash-grey, and crunches like old snow. Dead trees stand bone-white, still upright after nobody knows how long.\n\nNo bird sings out here. By noon your own footsteps are the loudest thing for miles.\n\nYou are walking point when you stop, and crouch.\n\nIn one of the hoof-scratches lies a chip of black glass, worn smooth by a thumb."},{"t":"act","label":"PICK IT UP"},{"t":"say","text":"You turn it over in your palm. It is no bigger than a fingernail: the kind of thing a child carries for luck.\n\nFifty paces on, there is another.\n\nShe is dropping them."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"The dead trees are still standing.","second":"Nothing here has rotted. Nothing has lived here to rot them."},"Agility":{"first":"Each chip lies where a horse slowed for a rise.","second":"She picks her moments."},"Intellect":{"first":"She has a pocketful, and a long way to go.","second":"She is spacing them. She is counting."},"Charm":{"first":"The men who have her have not noticed a child's hand opening and closing.","second":"She has made herself very easy to overlook."},"Craft":{"first":"That ridge ahead has a corner on it.","second":"Rock does not weather square."},"Aim":{"first":"A hundred yards off the riders' line there is a shadow that is too straight.","second":"Nothing out here is straight unless somebody made it so."}}},{"t":"say","text":"It is a doorway, cut into the side of a ridge: squared, deliberate, half buried under a fall of rock. The riders went by a hundred yards away, and never turned their heads."},{"t":"choice","id":0,"labels":["KEEP TO THE TRAIL","GO TO THE DOORWAY"],"mode":"pick","branches":[{"options":[0],"text":"You stay on the hoof-scratches for another mile, and find a third chip, and bring it back. {F1} and {F3} are already at the fall of rock, with their sleeves rolled."},{"options":[1],"text":"You go to the fall of rock with the others and stand looking at it. {F2} keeps on along the trail, and comes back within the hour with a third chip in hand."}]},{"t":"challenge","title":"THE BURIED DOORWAY","desc":"One wrong stone, and the rest of the fall comes with it.","options":[{"attr":"Craft","verb":"work out which stones can come away"},{"attr":"Might","verb":"shift the biggest of them, and trust the rest to hold"}],"reward":"+500g","fail":"half the fall comes down"},{"t":"say","text":"Stone by stone the fall comes away, and what is left above it holds. A thin trickle of grit runs down, and stops. The way opens cleanly.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"Half the fall comes down with a roar and a choking cloud of black dust. When it clears, the doorway is open, and you are all the same colour.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"say","text":"Inside is a room cut from the ridge. Old soot blackens its ceiling, from fires that went out centuries ago. Cut into the walls at sleeping height, facing each other across the floor, is a row of niches, each just long enough for a person to lie in. The air in here is cool, and smells of nothing at all.\n\nFor a moment nobody goes any further in.\n\nWhoever wrote your fragments slept here, walking this same country, a long time ago.\n\nIn a crack in the nearest niche is a single die, carved from bone, its spots worn almost smooth by somebody's fingers.\n\nThey had long nights here too.\n\nBetween the niches, at chest height, is a housing."},{"t":"act","label":"LAY YOUR HAND ON IT"},{"t":"say","text":"Its face slides back with a low grate of stone. The ridge has been warm under your hand all day. The cold that comes out of the housing is older than the soot on the ceiling.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"Nobody has been in here for a very long time. And the riders passed a hundred yards away, and never knew."},{"t":"say","text":"At dusk there is smoke, from a hut in a fold of the ridges to the north-east."},{"t":"say","text":"That night you sleep where they slept, and build your fire in their doorway against the cold. Garrick pours out the last of the day's tea, one more cup than there are people, and sets the extra one down at the empty place.\n\nYour own fire, in the doorway, shows just as plainly as theirs did."},{"t":"say","text":"**She is alive, and she is thinking. The hut, at first light.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE BLACK RIDGES** · Day 4","You earned: `[gold]` · Craft or Might `[growth]`","You learned: **Wren is alive.** She is dropping her glass chips for whoever comes after, and the men who have her have not noticed. And the people who wrote your fragments once slept in a room the riders rode straight past. They had long nights too.","You hold: three of Wren's chips","Fragments: 4 found","Tomorrow: **the shepherd's hut, at first light**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":24,"wAtk":17,"fightReward":0}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 3, 5, $json${"week":3,"day":5,"title":"The shepherd's hut","heading":"The shepherd's hut","question":"is she in the hut?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"First light finds you on the last ridge above it. You can hear the spring before you see it: the first running water since Ashcombe.\n\nIn a fold of the ridges a spring runs out of the black rock, and round it the world remembers how to be green: grass, a stand of trees, and a low stone hut with a sod roof.\n\nThere are two ways down to it."},{"t":"choice","id":0,"labels":["THE RIDERS' LINE","WREN'S LINE"],"mode":"pick","branches":[{"options":[0],"text":"The hoof-scratches go the long way, round the head of the fold. You follow them in, in the open. {F2} takes the goat-track that her chips mark, and comes down it with five more in hand."},{"options":[1],"text":"Her chips mark something shorter: a goat-track straight down through the rocks, which nobody on a horse could take. You find five more of them on the way. She walked this part."}]},{"t":"say","text":"On the ridge above the hut a grey coat stands up from among the rocks, where he was left behind to watch.\n\nHe comes down to meet you, and he takes his time about it."},{"t":"fight","name":"THE GREY COAT ON THE RIDGE","desc":"Polite, and in good boots.","firstLines":["You came by her track: you are on him before he has seen you.","You came by the open line: he has been watching you for some time."],"strikeFirst":{"on":"choice","choice":0,"options":[1]}},{"t":"say","text":"He goes back up the way he came, without a word, onto the bare black rock, and the rock takes no prints. By the time you reach the top of the rise there is nothing on the ridge but the wind."},{"t":"say","text":"He goes without his hat. It is a good hat. Inside the band somebody has stitched two letters, very small, the way a mother would.","cond":{"on":"fight","won":true}},{"t":"say","text":"The hut is empty.\n\nThe door stands open. A thread of smoke is still going up from the roof-hole into the morning."},{"t":"choice","id":1,"labels":["LOW ON THE DOORFRAME","THE BEAM OVER THE PALLET","THE FIRE"],"mode":"each","branches":[{"options":[0],"text":"Scratched fresh into the wood, at a child's height, with something small and sharp: **WREN.**\n\nThe letters are small and pressed hard, and each one has been gone over twice. You run your thumb down them. The wood is still pale in the cuts."},{"options":[2],"text":"A pot is still on it, and catching. A tin cup lies on its side where it was dropped. There is a blanket, folded with care, and beside it a second one, thrown down.\n\nThey were here within the hour. And they left at a run."},{"options":[1],"text":"Cut deep and neat into the old beam over the pallet, in a grown hand, dark with years of smoke:\n\n*Until the throne rise whole.*\n\nThe words that ended the Order's scripture under the mill hill. The words they chanted over Corin while the knife was out. Whoever sleeps here has said them every night for a long time."}]},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"The door was not pulled shut behind them. It was left swinging.","second":"They did not stop to close it."},"Agility":{"first":"By the spring, the grass is still lifting where it was trodden.","second":"Not long. Not long at all."},"Intellect":{"first":"A folded blanket and a dropped cup, in the same room.","second":"Somebody careful, who stopped being careful all at once."},"Charm":{"first":"The pallet is by the fire: the warm place.","second":"They gave her the best bed in the house."},"Craft":{"first":"The sod roof has been patched in three different years.","second":"This hut is kept. Somebody comes back to it."},"Aim":{"first":"High on the black rock, a scuff of pale dust where a boot turned.","second":"Then nothing."}}},{"t":"say","text":"Until today, these people have never once hurried."},{"t":"say","text":"From the doorway you can see straight back across the ridges to the one you slept under last night.\n\nThey saw your fire."},{"t":"say","text":"Garrick crouches by the hearth and lays his palm flat over the ashes. *\"They're always a step ahead of us.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"The hut is newer than what it stands on. Under the hearthstone the footing is older, bigger stonework. Set into it:"},{"t":"act","label":"BRUSH YOUR HAND ACROSS IT"},{"t":"say","text":"The fire's heat is still in the stone above. What is inside is as cold as well-water.\n\n**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**","fragment":true},{"t":"say","text":"**A step, now, and no more. If they could see you, can you see them? The cairn on the highest ridge, before the light goes.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE SHEPHERD'S HUT** · Day 5","You earned: `[gold]`","You learned: she was here **within the hour**, and **they left at a run**. Her name is scratched in the doorframe in her own hand. Over her bed, cut long ago: *Until the throne rise whole.*","You hold: eight of Wren's chips","Fragments: 5 found","Tomorrow: **the cairn, before the light goes**"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":24,"wAtk":17,"fightReward":300}$json$::jsonb),
('dark-moon', 1, 3, 6, $json${"week":3,"day":6,"title":"The cairn","heading":"The cairn","question":"where have they taken her?","steps":[{"t":"say","text":"All afternoon the cairn has been in sight: a dark knuckle of piled stones far off on the skyline, that never seems to come any nearer. Every ridge you cross shows you another between you and it. The shadows are long now, and reaching.\n\nThe cairn stands on the highest ridge in the burned country, and the light is going."},{"t":"notice","lines":{"Might":{"first":"The lowest stones of that cairn are as big as sheep.","second":"Nobody carried those up there for a landmark."},"Agility":{"first":"The wind is rising as the light goes.","second":"In an hour that ridge will be no place to stand."},"Intellect":{"first":"The Blackglass, the buried room and the hut lie in a line.","second":"A line points somewhere."},"Charm":{"first":"Nobody has said her name all day.","second":"There are eight of her chips among you."},"Craft":{"first":"One hill out there is too round.","second":"The others were worn down. That one was melted."},"Aim":{"first":"Over one hill, and only one, the air is moving like the air over a forge.","second":"Something under that hill is still hot."}}},{"t":"challenge","title":"THE CLIMB","desc":"There is an hour of light, and more than an hour of ridge.","options":[{"attr":"Might","verb":"straight up the face"},{"attr":"Agility","verb":"along the knife-edge, where it is shorter and worse"}],"reward":"+500g","fail":"you get there in the dark, and see nothing but what you carry"},{"t":"say","text":"You come up beside the cairn with the sun still on the ridges, and the whole burned country is spread out under you: the Blackglass shining dully to the west, the green fold of the hut far below.\n\nAnd one hill unlike all the others. Round, and black, with a crack across its crown, where the air above it shimmers as if the hill were breathing.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"The last of the ridge you climb by feel, with the wind pulling at your coat and the rock still warm under your hands.\n\nIt is full dark when you reach the cairn. There is nothing to see from it but black on black, and the stars.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"say","text":"The last fragment is at the cairn's foot: not hidden, only wedged between the lowest stones, where a careless boot would miss it."},{"t":"act","label":"TAKE IT"},{"t":"say","text":"**A locked Seeker Fragment has been added to your Chest.**\n\nThat is six.","fragment":true},{"t":"act","label":"LAY THEM OUT"},{"t":"say","text":"They settle, as they have twice before. The wind worries at their edges, and they do not lift. A map, old and exact, with a ridgeline drawn along its top."},{"t":"act","label":"TURN IT TO THE SKYLINE"},{"t":"say","text":"You turn it until the drawn ridges sit on the real ones. They fit. And the place the map ends is the round hill with the crack in its crown. You were looking at it before the map told you.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":true}},{"t":"say","text":"You turn it until the drawn ridges sit on the black shapes against the stars. They fit. The place the map ends is a round hill you can only just make out, with a notch in its crown.","cond":{"on":"challenge","pass":false}},{"t":"say","text":"*\"The Kiln,\"* Garrick says. *\"That's the shepherds' name for it.\"*"},{"t":"say","text":"In through the crack. Down a way cut long ago. To a room beneath the hill."},{"t":"say","text":"The others are still coming up the last of the slope below you, too far down to see what you hold."},{"t":"choice","id":0,"labels":["READ IT OUT","LET {F1} READ IT"],"mode":"flavor","branches":[]},{"t":"say","text":"It is said aloud, twice, for the ones on the slope below. The wind takes every word of it down the ridge."},{"t":"say","text":"The cold comes up fast once the sun is gone. Garrick builds the fire up, and gives whoever is shivering hardest the warm side of it."},{"t":"say","text":"Not an hour after full dark, far below: a single lamp, moving across the black ground toward the Kiln.\n\nIt reaches the foot of the hill. It climbs. And it goes out.\n\nNot blown out. Gone in."},{"t":"say","text":"**Whatever happens under that hill has started. Into the Kiln, tonight.**","pull":true},{"t":"summary","lines":["**THE CAIRN** · Day 6","You earned: `[gold]` · Might or Agility `[growth]`","You learned: **the Kiln.** A round black hill that breathes warm air through a crack in its crown. The map goes in through that crack, to a room beneath. A lamp has just gone in ahead of you.","*On a failure:* You missed something at the cairn. Someone at the fire may have seen it.","You hold: the map · eight of Wren's chips","Fragments: 6 of 6 · the map is whole","Tomorrow: **THE GATHERING** · down through the Kiln's crown, together"]}]}$json$::jsonb, $json${"dc":7,"wDef":24,"wAtk":17,"fightReward":0}$json$::jsonb)
